---
import { AccessDeniedError } from '../../../lib/api';
import AsyncState from '../../ui/AsyncState.vue';
import DesignSection from '../DesignSection.astro';
import OverlayDemo from '../OverlayDemo.vue';
import Stage from '../Stage.astro';

const DENIED = new AccessDeniedError('Your account has not been granted access to this platform yet. Ask an administrator.', null);

// The props every state shares; each example turns one on.
const IDLE = {
  loading: false,
  error: null,
  errorTitle: 'Usage unavailable',
  sessionExpired: false,
  accessDenied: null,
};
---

<DesignSection id="dialog">
  <Fragment slot="definition"> A dialog interrupts for a decision that cannot be undone or a short form. A tooltip names an icon or shows an exact value. </Fragment>
  <OverlayDemo client:load />
  <div class="design-prose">
    <ul>
      <li>Dialog buttons sit bottom right, with the confirming action last. The confirming button repeats the title's verb. The title is the 20px step.</li>
      <li>A tooltip never holds information a person needs to complete the task. It is not reachable on touch.</li>
      <li>Prefer inline content to a dialog. Do not open a dialog from a dialog.</li>
      <li>A tooltip is flat: page background, strong border, 4px radius. It uses the native Popover API, so a scrolling ancestor cannot clip it.</li>
    </ul>
  </div>
  <p class="af-help">Used on: Tokens (new, revoke), Identities (unlink, consent), Admin (maintenance mode). Tooltips: badges, dates, icon-only buttons.</p>
</DesignSection>

<DesignSection id="empty">
  <Fragment slot="definition">
    When a list has nothing in it, say what belongs there and offer the action that fills it. Data fetched from the broker goes through one ladder of states (<code>AsyncState</code>): loading, session expired, access denied, error, empty, then the content.
  </Fragment>
  <Stage label="Empty state">
    <div class="empty border-input border">
      <header>
        <h4>No tokens yet</h4>
        <p>Tokens let clients that can't sign in with a browser, such as Claude Desktop, reach the gateway as you.</p>
      </header>
      <section>
        <button type="button" class="btn">New token</button>
      </section>
    </div>
  </Stage>
  <div class="design-cols">
    <Stage label="AsyncState: loading">
      <AsyncState {...IDLE} loading={true} loadingLabel="Loading usage…" />
    </Stage>
    <Stage label="AsyncState: session expired">
      <AsyncState {...IDLE} sessionExpired={true} inline />
    </Stage>
    <Stage label="AsyncState: access denied">
      <AsyncState {...IDLE} accessDenied={DENIED} inline />
    </Stage>
    <Stage label="AsyncState: error">
      <AsyncState {...IDLE} error="The broker did not answer. Try again in a minute." inline />
    </Stage>
  </div>
  <Stage label="AsyncState: empty">
    <AsyncState {...IDLE} empty={true}>
      <header slot="empty">
        <h4>No tool calls in the last 30 days</h4>
        <p>Once your AI assistant calls tools through this platform, its estimated context usage shows up here.</p>
      </header>
    </AsyncState>
  </Stage>
  <p class="af-help">
    This is Basecoat's <code>empty</code>, which centres its content under a dashed border; the portal keeps that layout. An empty state may carry the page's primary button, so the page header does not repeat it. The failure states are shown as notes here (<code>inline</code>); a page uses the banner form when the page's own data fails to load. Used on: Tokens, Identities, Usage (no calls in range).
  </p>
</DesignSection>
